# Common Structure

`src/common/` — shared (cross-module) primitives only.

## Target Shape

```text
src/
  common/
    exceptions/          # DomainException, DtoFailed
    types/               # generics, enums (New<T>, PaginatedResult, Platform, ...)
    utils/               # pure helpers, no I/O (deepMerge)
    validators/          # class-validator helpers (IsNullable)
    decorators/          # cross-cutting decorators (ValidateDto)
    infra/
      prisma/            # PrismaModule, PrismaService, PrismaConnector,
                       # models/, schema.prisma, migrations/,
                       # TransactionRunner, TransactionContext
  http/                  # top-level — controllers, filters, guards, pipes
  modules/               # business modules
```

## Classification Table

| Artifact | Folder |
| --- | --- |
| Base exceptions (DomainException, DtoFailed) | `common/exceptions/` |
| Shared type, enum, generic | `common/types/` |
| Pure helper, no I/O | `common/utils/` |
| Reusable `class-validator` helper | `common/validators/` |
| Cross-cutting method decorator | `common/decorators/` |
| Prisma infra (module, models, migrations, txn) | `common/infra/prisma/` |
| HTTP controller / filter / guard / pipe | `src/http/` (TOP-LEVEL) |
| Module domain exceptions | `modules/{m}/domain/exceptions/` |

## Rules

- Each folder has `index.ts` barrel.
- Import via `@common/{folder}` barrel — never deep paths.
- Prisma models live in `common/infra/prisma/models/` — NOT in module `domain/`.
- Prisma access: `this.prisma.db` (via `PrismaService`).
- HTTP is TOP-LEVEL (`src/http/`) — not in `common/`.

## Import Paths (always via barrel)

| What | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Types, enums, generics | `@common/types` |
| `DomainException`, `DtoFailed` | `@common/exceptions` |
| Pure helpers | `@common/utils` |
| `ValidateDto` | `@common/decorators` |
| `IsNullable` | `@common/validators` |
| Prisma module / service / transaction | `@common/infra/prisma` |

Good: `import { PrismaService } from '@common/infra/prisma'`  
Bad: `import { PrismaService } from '@common/infra/prisma/prisma.service'`

## DomainException

```ts
// common/exceptions/domain.exception.ts
export abstract class DomainException extends Error {
  constructor(params: {
    code: string
    message: string
    cause?: Error
    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>
  }) {
    super(
      params.message,
      params.cause ? { cause: params.cause } : undefined,
    )
    this.code = params.code
    this.metadata = params.metadata
  }
  public readonly code: string
  public readonly metadata?: Record<string, unknown>
}
```

## Anti-Patterns

- Standalone files in `common/` root → classify and put in subfolder
- HTTP code in `common/infra/` → top-level
- Prisma models in `modules/{m}/domain/` → `common/infra/prisma/models/`
- Module exceptions in `common/exceptions/` → module's `domain/exceptions/`
- Empty NestJS module for a single provider → register directly in infra module
- Deep import path → use barrel
- Cross-subfolder re-export → each barrel exports only its own content

## Checklist

- [ ] File in correct folder (see table)
- [ ] Import via `@common/{folder}` barrel, not deep path
- [ ] Prisma models NOT in `modules/*/domain/`
- [ ] Module exceptions NOT in `common/exceptions/`
- [ ] No orphan files in `common/` root
- [ ] HTTP code NOT in `common/`
- [ ] Each subfolder has `index.ts`
